      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we need to express $473_{10}$ in base $8$. This means we need to repeatedly divide $473$ by $8$ and keep track of the remainders.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\\[ 473 \\div 8 = 59 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\nSo, the least significant digit (rightmost digit) of the base $8$ representation is $1$.\n\nNext, we take the quotient $59$ and divide it by $8$:\n\\[ 59 \\div 8 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 3. \\]\nSo, the next digit in the base $8$ representation is $3$.\n\nNext, we take the quotient $7$ and divide it by $8$:\n\\[ 7 \\div 8 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 7. \\]\nSo, the next digit in the base $8$ representation is $7$.\n\nSince the quotient is now $0$, we stop the process. Reading the remainders from bottom to top, the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $731_8$.\n\nThe first digit of the base $8$ representation is $7$. Therefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
